  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Envelope 2013: Pro-poor REDD (IUCN), ph. 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program aims at securing a poverty reduction focus in REDD+ (Reduced Emission from Degradation and Deforestation) porgrams being implemented in Ghana, Cameroun, Uganda, Indonesia and Guatemala. The selected countries represent the major regions for REDD+ implementation and all five countries have REDD+ programs under implementation. This second and final phase of the program will further analyse lessons learnt from phase I and will through implementation in an additional forest regions in each country add new experiences and lessons. The program further aims at influencing the global concept of REDD+ with special focus on the right of forest dependent communities including the economic and social development aspirations of these communities.</narrative>
  </description>
